#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:29
msgid "Handling WebSocket connections in Node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:31
msgid ""
"You can handle WebSockets on the server side by listening for HTTP "
"Upgrade requests, and creating a new socket for the request. This socket "
"object exposes the usual WebSocket methods for receiving and sending "
"messages. For example this is how you'd implement an echo server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:60
msgid ""
"`WebSocket` objects are also duplex streams, so you could replace the "
"`ws.on('message', ...)` line with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:67
msgid ""
"Note that under certain circumstances (notably a draft-76 client "
"connecting through an HTTP proxy), the WebSocket handshake will not be "
"complete after you call `new WebSocket()` because the server will not "
"have received the entire handshake from the client yet. In this case, "
"calls to `ws.send()` will buffer the message in memory until the "
"handshake is complete, at which point any buffered messages will be sent "
"to the client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:74
msgid ""
"If you need to detect when the WebSocket handshake is complete, you can "
"use the `onopen` event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:77
msgid ""
"If the connection's protocol version supports it, you can call "
"`ws.ping()` to send a ping message and wait for the client's response. "
"This method takes a message string, and an optional callback that fires "
"when a matching pong message is received. It returns `true` if and only "
"if a ping message was sent. If the client does not support ping/pong, "
"this method sends no data and returns `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:91
msgid "Using the WebSocket client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:93
msgid ""
"The client supports both the plain-text `ws` protocol and the encrypted "
"`wss` protocol, and has exactly the same interface as a socket you would "
"use in a web browser. On the wire it identifies itself as `hybi-13`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:116
msgid ""
"The WebSocket client also lets you inspect the status and headers of the "
"handshake response via its `statusCode` and `headers` properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:119
msgid ""
"To connect via a proxy, set the `proxy` option to the HTTP origin of the "
"proxy, including any authorization information, custom headers and TLS "
"config you require. Only the `origin` setting is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:133
msgid ""
"The `tls` value is a Node 'TLS options' object that will be passed to "
"[`tls.connect()`](http://nodejs.org/api/tls.html#tls_tls_connect_options_callback)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:137
msgid "Subprotocol negotiation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:139
msgid ""
"The WebSocket protocol allows peers to select and identify the "
"application protocol to use over the connection. On the client side, you "
"can set which protocols the client accepts by passing a list of protocol "
"names when you construct the socket:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:148
msgid ""
"On the server side, you can likewise pass in the list of protocols the "
"server supports after the other constructor arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:155
msgid ""
"If the client and server agree on a protocol, both the client- and "
"server-side socket objects expose the selected protocol through the "
"`ws.protocol` property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:159
msgid "Protocol extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:161
msgid ""
"faye-websocket is based on the [websocket-"
"extensions](https://github.com/faye/websocket-extensions-node) framework "
"that allows extensions to be negotiated via the `Sec-WebSocket-"
"Extensions` header. To add extensions to a connection, pass an array of "
"extensions to the `:extensions` option. For example, to add [permessage-"
"deflate](https://github.com/faye/permessage-deflate-node):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:175
msgid "Initialization options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:177
msgid ""
"Both the server- and client-side classes allow an options object to be "
"passed in at initialization time, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:185
msgid ""
"`protocols` is an array of subprotocols as described above, or `null`. "
"`options` is an optional object containing any of these fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:188
msgid ""
"`extensions` - an array of [websocket-extensions](https://github.com/faye"
"/websocket-extensions-node) compatible extensions, as described above"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:191
msgid ""
"`headers` - an object containing key-value pairs representing HTTP "
"headers to be sent during the handshake process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:193
msgid ""
"`maxLength` - the maximum allowed size of incoming message frames, in "
"bytes. The default value is `2^26 - 1`, or 1 byte short of 64 MiB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:195
msgid ""
"`ping` - an integer that sets how often the WebSocket should send ping "
"frames, measured in seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:198
msgid "The client accepts some additional options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:200
msgid "`proxy` - settings for a proxy as described above"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:201
msgid ""
"`tls` - a Node 'TLS options' object containing TLS settings for the "
"origin server, this will be passed to "
"[`tls.connect()`](http://nodejs.org/api/tls.html#tls_tls_connect_options_callback)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:204
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`ca` - (legacy) a shorthand for passing `{tls: {ca: value}}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:207
msgid "WebSocket API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:209
msgid ""
"Both server- and client-side `WebSocket` objects support the following "
"API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:211
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<b>`on('open', function(event) {})`</b> fires when the socket connection "
"is established. Event has no attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:213
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<b>`on('message', function(event) {})`</b> fires when the socket receives"
" a message. Event has one attribute, <b>`data`</b>, which is either a "
"`String` (for text frames) or a `Buffer` (for binary frames)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:216
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<b>`on('error', function(event) {})`</b> fires when there is a protocol "
"error due to bad data sent by the other peer. This event is purely "
"informational, you do not need to implement error recover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:219
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<b>`on('close', function(event) {})`</b> fires when either the client or "
"the server closes the connection. Event has two optional attributes, "
"<b>`code`</b> and <b>`reason`</b>, that expose the status code and "
"message sent by the peer that closed the connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:223
msgid ""
"<b>`send(message)`</b> accepts either a `String` or a `Buffer` and sends "
"a text or binary message over the connection to the other peer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:225
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<b>`ping(message, function() {})`</b> sends a ping frame with an optional"
" message and fires the callback when a matching pong is received."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:227
msgid ""
"<b>`close(code, reason)`</b> closes the connection, sending the given "
"status code and reason text, both of which are optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:229
msgid ""
"<b>`version`</b> is a string containing the version of the `WebSocket` "
"protocol the connection is using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:231
msgid ""
"<b>`protocol`</b> is a string (which may be empty) identifying the "
"subprotocol the socket is using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:235
msgid "Handling EventSource connections in Node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:237
msgid ""
"EventSource connections provide a very similar interface, although "
"because they only allow the server to send data to the client, there is "
"no `onmessage` API. EventSource allows the server to push text messages "
"to the client, where each message has an optional event-type and ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:272
msgid ""
"The `send` method takes two optional parameters, `event` and `id`. The "
"default event-type is `'message'` with no ID. For example, to send a "
"`notification` event with ID `99`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:280
msgid "The `EventSource` object exposes the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:282
msgid ""
"<b>`url`</b> is a string containing the URL the client used to create the"
" EventSource."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:284
msgid ""
"<b>`lastEventId`</b> is a string containing the last event ID received by"
" the client. You can use this when the client reconnects after a dropped "
"connection to determine which messages need resending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:288
msgid ""
"When you initialize an EventSource with ` new EventSource()`, you can "
"pass configuration options after the `response` parameter. Available "
"options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:291
msgid ""
"<b>`headers`</b> is an object containing custom headers to be set on the "
"EventSource response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:293
msgid ""
"<b>`retry`</b> is a number that tells the client how long (in seconds) it"
" should wait after a dropped connection before attempting to reconnect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:295
msgid ""
"<b>`ping`</b> is a number that tells the server how often (in seconds) to"
" send 'ping' packets to the client to keep the connection open, to defeat"
" timeouts set by proxies. The client will ignore these messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:299
msgid ""
"For example, this creates a connection that allows access from any "
"origin, pings every 15 seconds and is retryable every 10 seconds if the "
"connection is broken:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faye-websocket_README.md:310
msgid ""
"You can send a ping message at any time by calling `es.ping()`. Unlike "
"WebSocket, the client does not send a response to this; it is merely to "
"send some data over the wire to keep the connection alive."
msgstr ""

